    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17572" root="زحم" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُحْمٌ</span></b> , with damm, a name of <i>Mekkeh:</i> (K, *
TA:) so says Th: but ISd says that the name
commonly known is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُحْم</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُّ رُحْمٍ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُّ الرُّحْمِ</span>]:
(TA:) or it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُّ الزُّحْمِ</span> [probably, I think, a
mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُّ الرُّحْمِ</span>]. (K, TA.)

